---
/**
 * Frequently asked questions, from the README (Install, Requirements, Lossless,
 * Privacy, "Why Stash isn't on the Play Store", "When background sync stops
 * working") and checked against the app's code; keep them in step.
 *
 * The free, Play Store, lossless and requirements answers were corrected
 * against the app in October 2026, and the README with them. When the README
 * and the app disagree, the app's code is right.
 *
 * Each answer has an id (faq-*) so other pages can link straight to it;
 * browsers open the question when its answer is linked.
 */
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../../data/site';
---

<section class="section faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container layout">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="overline">FAQ</p>
      <h2 id="faq-title" class="section-title">Questions, answered</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Didn't find yours? The Discord is the place to ask, and answers come fast.</p>
      <a class="button button-secondary ask" href={LINKS.discord}>
        <Icon name="discord" size="20px" />
        Ask on Discord
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="list">
      <details>
        <summary>Is Stash free?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-free">
          <p>
            Yes. Stash is free and open source under the
            <a href={LINKS.license}>GNU General Public License, version 3</a> or later. There's no Stash account to
            make, but to sync a library you need your own Spotify and/or YouTube Music account.
          </p>
          <p>If you'd like to help keep Stash going, you can <a href="#community">support the project</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why isn't Stash on the Play Store?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-play-store">
          <p>Google Play doesn't allow apps that save audio from YouTube, so Stash is published on GitHub instead.</p>
          <p>
            Stash never downloads audio from Spotify. It reads your Spotify library with your own login and finds
            each song's audio elsewhere, as the <a href="/privacy#what-stash-talks-to">privacy page</a> lists. Stash
            isn't affiliated with or endorsed by any of the services it connects to, and you're responsible for how
            you use it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do I install it?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-install">
          <p>
            On your phone, open the <a href={LINKS.latestRelease}>latest release</a> and download the
            <code>.apk</code> file. Open it, and if Android warns about installs from unknown sources, allow them
            for your browser and try again. Then tap Install.
          </p>
          <p>
            Stash checks GitHub for new releases and lets you know when one is out. To get updates through
            <a href={LINKS.obtainium}>Obtainium</a>, add <code>https://github.com/rawnaldclark/Stash</code> to it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Where does lossless come from?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-lossless">
          <p>There's no Qobuz account or token inside the app. FLAC can come from:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Your own Qobuz account</strong>, connected in Settings › Audio &amp; Quality. Your email
              and password are sent once to Qobuz to mint a token; Stash keeps the token, not the password.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Your own relay endpoint</strong>, if you run one, set under Advanced on the same screen.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Stash's relay</strong>, in official release builds only, when nothing of your own is connected
              or working. The <a href="/privacy#lossless-and-fallback-audio">privacy page</a> says what it's sent.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            When no lossless source can serve a song, it streams in AAC or Opus instead, and Now Playing shows where
            it came from. Downloads wait for FLAC by default and show as "Waiting for lossless". To take an AAC or
            Opus copy instead, turn on Lossy fallback in Settings › Audio &amp; Quality.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is my data safe?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-privacy">
          <p>
            Stash has no account server, no analytics and no third-party crash reporters. Your credentials live on
            your phone, with the Spotify, YouTube and Discord tokens encrypted (AES-256-GCM, via Google's
            <a href={LINKS.tink}>Tink</a>), and each one is only ever sent back to the service it came from. No
            host the project runs ever sees one.
          </p>
          <p>
            Lyrics, scrobbling, artist info and lossless have hosts of their own. The
            <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> lists everything Stash can reach, and what each one is sent. Found
            a security issue? Please <a href={LINKS.security}>report it privately</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What do I need?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-requirements">
          <p>
            A phone running Android 8.0 or later, and a Spotify and/or YouTube Music account. With Download on, you
            also need room for your music. FLAC files are large: a four-minute song is about 28 MB in CD quality and
            about 70 MB in Hi-Res, and you can pick the quality in Settings › Audio &amp; Quality. Stream only needs
            almost nothing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Sync stops in the background. What can I do?<Icon name="chevron-down" class="chevron" /></summary>
        <div class="answer" id="faq-background-sync">
          <p>
            Some phones, especially from Samsung, Xiaomi, OnePlus and Huawei, close background apps aggressively
            to save battery. If a sync fails partway with a foreground-service error, open your phone's Settings ›
            Apps › Stash › Battery and set it to Unrestricted. You only need to do this once.
          </p>
          <p>
            If that's not enough on your phone, <a href={LINKS.dontKillMyApp}>dontkillmyapp.com</a> has steps for
            each manufacturer.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: clamp(40px, 6vw, 96px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .intro {
    position: sticky;
    top: 112px;
  }

  .ask {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  details {
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    background: var(--glass);
    transition:
      background-color 200ms ease,
      border-color 200ms ease;
  }

  details:hover,
  details[open] {
    border-color: var(--glass-border-bright);
  }

  details[open] {
    background: var(--glass-hover);
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 20px 22px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1rem + 0.3vw, 1.25rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.3;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  summary :global(.chevron) {
    color: var(--text-2);
    transition: transform 200ms ease;
  }

  details[open] summary :global(.chevron) {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .answer {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 0 22px 22px;
    color: var(--text-2);
    scroll-margin-top: 160px;
  }

  .answer ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }

  .answer li::marker {
    color: var(--purple);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .layout {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .intro {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
